{"id":"u-248c6b40-9609-41b9-adad-a89c0362a44c","src":"community","title":"Science Based Full Body","author":"Ryan W.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/frXwmA-boostcamphypertrophyprogram","desc":"This 4-day full body program is designed to maximize muscle growth through high-frequency training, optimal volume distribution, and progressive overload. Each session targets all major muscle groups, ensuring balanced development while maintaining recovery efficiency throughout the week.\n\nThe program emphasizes top-set focused training, where key compound and isolation movements are pushed close to failure to drive mechanical tension and hypertrophy. Secondary work supports additional volume without excessive fatigue, allowing for consistent performance across all training days. Allow 1 warmup set, first top set at 9rpe, 2nd top set at 10rpe.\n\nRep ranges are strategically structured to combine strength and hypertrophy adaptations, typically ranging from moderate-heavy loading on compounds to higher-rep metabolic work on accessories. Exercise selection prioritizes stable, joint-friendly movements to improve execution quality and long-term progression.\n\nThis split is ideal for lifters who want:\n\nIncreased muscle-building frequency (each muscle 2–4x/week exposure)\nEfficient 60–75 minute sessions\nClear progressive overload structure\nA balance of intensity and recovery\n\nOverall, this program is built to drive consistent size and strength gains without unnecessary complexity—just hard, focused training executed with intent.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-06T22:06:03.655Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Quad & Chest Focus","Posterior Chain & Lats","Quad & Back Focus","Delts & Arms Focus"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"High Bar Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":9},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10}],"note":"Top 1 set @1 RIR